  {
    "slug": "fishy-illustration",
    "title": "Fish Illustration",
    "medium": "Gouache + colored pencil",
    "file": "fish.webp",
    "description": "",
    "thoughtProcess": [
      "I love drawing fish because they’re so colorful and generally have interesting shapes. There’s also a fluidity to how they move through water that makes them fun to draw. With this piece, the idea was to capture some of that movement and variety in a fun interpretation of fish.",
      "I was trying to move more into an illustration mindset, using flatter elements like the bubbles and lines to show the undercurrents you would see under the sea. This was also an exercise in drawing fish from many different perspectives and figuring out how to show their shapes from different angles."
    ],
    "links": [
      {
        "label": "View original post",
