  {
    "slug": "japanese-tea-garden-tree",
    "title": "A Japanese tea garden tree",
    "medium": "Drawing",
    "file": "japanese-tea-garden-tree.jpg",
    "description": "",
    "thoughtProcess": [
      "I’ve always struggled more with digital art because I usually use the material to help inspire the drawings I like to do. As someone who is color-forward, having access to an unlimited color palette can lead to a less curated drawing.",
      "This was the first drawing where it clicked for me to try a more illustrative approach. I wasn’t going to get the same textures as physical mediums with digital art, so I needed to create the texture myself through hatching and shading, and by creating interesting lines."
    ],
